Repair this bounded queue. It can exceed capacity when producers wake together and close() can strand consumers. Provide a complete implementation using threading.Condition, type hints, monotonic timeout handling, and tests for contention, timeout, close-before-get, and close-with-buffered-items. Define the close semantics clearly.

class Queue:
    def __init__(self, capacity):
        self.items=[]; self.capacity=capacity; self.cv=Condition()
    def put(self, item):
        with self.cv:
            if len(self.items) >= self.capacity: self.cv.wait()
            self.items.append(item); self.cv.notify()
    def get(self):
        with self.cv:
            if not self.items: self.cv.wait()
            return self.items.pop(0)
